counterfactuals.output:
A method of designing an aircraft propulsion system, the method comprising:

interactively defining, by one or more design tools, an aircraft engine and an associated nacelle as an integrated propulsion arrangement;

configuring the aircraft engine to include a fan, a core flowpath, a bypass flowpath, and a compressor system disposed downstream of the fan in the core flowpath;

configuring the compressor system to include at least a first compressor and a second compressor arranged to compress core airflow delivered thereto;

configuring the nacelle to at least partially surround the aircraft engine and to define, in cooperation with the aircraft engine, a bypass duct;

sizing and positioning the fan such that, during operation, the fan accelerates an incoming airflow and divides the accelerated airflow into a core airflow directed into the core flowpath and a bypass airflow directed through the bypass duct;

iteratively modifying one or more engine design parameters and one or more nacelle design parameters in response to performance, aerodynamic, structural, acoustic, installation, or efficiency criteria; and

selecting a combined engine-and-nacelle configuration based on the interactive design of the aircraft engine and the nacelle.
